Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.

The community you will join:

As a Staff Experience Designer, you will partner with supporting disciplines such as writers, researchers, product specialists and engineers to build beautiful, usable, forward-looking products that empower people. Our design charter is to help foster an emotional connection with our community, keeping usability and accessibility as our prime virtues. We do our best to practice inclusive design at every turn, spanning both the online and offline experiences we create for our community.

The difference you will make:&nbsp;

As a Staff Experience Designer in London, you will play a critical role in shaping how Airbnb shows up in markets across EMEA, Latin America, and APAC. You will help ensure our global products feel truly local-adapting core experiences to regional needs while feeding market insights back into the broader product strategy. Sitting at the intersection of product, design, and regional strategy, you will work across time zones and functions to define and deliver an international roadmap that spans both tactical UI improvements and larger strategic bets. You will bring a high bar for visual and interaction design craft, model AI-enabled ways of working, and provide senior design leadership in a space that is growing in complexity and impact for Airbnb globally. The Staff Experience Designer is an individual contributor (IC) role that will report to a Manager or Director of Experience Design.&nbsp;

A typical day:&nbsp;

• Support and shape the evolution of the Airbnb platform from a design perspective; ensure consistency with, and contribute to, our brand architecture and product architecture.&nbsp;

• Partner with Product Managers, Engineers, Data Scientist, Researchers and Writers to define problems &amp; goals, map user flows, prototype interactions, and launch new products and services.

• Influence leadership decision making through a clear point of view and define and solve highly complex problems autonomously.&nbsp;

• Provide indirect leadership and mentorship for a team of designers through the end-to-end interaction and visual design of products and services for a global audience.

• Anticipate business challenges and independently create product solutions. Indirectly lead the work of a team of talented designers, writers, program managers, researchers, product managers and engineers as the defacto creative director of innovative projects

• Build strong relationships with leaders inside and outside of core product teams; strong communication and executive stakeholder management skills.

• Have a keen understanding of the technological, business and user opportunities and constraints.&nbsp;

• Scopes project work (in partnership with PMs and engineers) and helps define the design process and timeline.

Your expertise:&nbsp;

• Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and progressive experience

• Designer/Design Leader with 10+ years of experience.&nbsp;

• Excellent visual and interaction skills and craft.

• Defines the design direction and process and can lead others through it.

• Can accurately scope their work as well as their teammate's.

• Can effortlessly motivate and drive small to medium teams to transform a product.

• Demonstrated ability to help a team navigate ambiguity, set vision, and set strategy for global products.

• Systems-thinker with the ability to think beyond the pixels and design for offline experiences.

• Experience with making complex information, tools, and services easily digestible for your audience.

